{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZhEWkt1U7UBcSbeSkRHGx","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t// The `responses` protocol (OpenAI Responses API; OpenRouter): a pure\n     2\t// request encoder and stream decoder (spec 06, 2.6.2 and 2.8.2).\n     3\t\n     4\timport {\n     5\t    IncompleteStreamError,\n     6\t    ProviderError,\n     7\t} from './errors.js'\n     8\timport { wellFormed } from './json.js'\n     9\timport { responsesSystemMode } from './models.js'\n    10\timport type { SseEvent } from './sse.js'\n    11\timport { trimSlashes, type EncodeConfig, type EncodeRequest } from './chat.js'\n    12\timport type {\n    13\t    AssistantPart,\n    14\t    FinishReason,\n    15\t    ModelTurn,\n    16\t} from './types.js'\n    17\timport { normalizeUsage, responsesUsage } from './usage.js'\n    18\t\n    19\texport function responsesUrl (baseUrl:string):string {\n    20\t    return `${trimSlashes(baseUrl)}/responses`\n    21\t}\n    22\t\n    23\tfunction input (model:string, req:EncodeRequest):unknown[] {\n    24\t    const out:unknown[] = []\n    25\t    const mode = responsesSystemMode(model)\n    26\t    if (req.system !== '' && mode !== 'remove') {\n    27\t        out.push({ role:mode, content:req.system })\n    28\t    }\n    29\t    for (const item of req.items) {\n    30\t        if (item.role === 'user') {\n    31\t            out.push({\n    32\t                role:'user',\n    33\t                content:[{ type:'input_text', text:item.text }],\n    34\t            })\n    35\t        } else if (item.role === 'assistant') {\n    36\t            for (const p of item.parts) {\n    37\t                if (p.type === 'text') {\n    38\t                    out.push({ role:'assistant', content:p.text })\n    39\t                } else if (p.type === 'tool-call') {\n    40\t                    out.push({\n    41\t                        type:'function_call',\n    42\t                        call_id:p.id,\n    43\t                        name:p.name,\n    44\t                        arguments:p.input,\n    45\t                    })\n    46\t                }\n    47\t                // Reasoning is never replayed.\n    48\t            }\n    49\t        } else {\n    50\t            for (const r of item.results) {\n    51\t                out.push({\n    52\t                    type:'function_call_output',\n    53\t                    call_id:r.callId,\n    54\t                    output:r.output,\n    55\t                })\n    56\t            }\n    57\t        }\n    58\t    }\n    59\t    return out\n    60\t}\n    61\t\n    62\t// The request body. `store` is always false and the whole conversation is\n    63\t// replayed: no `previous_response_id`, `include`, or `reasoning`.\n    64\texport function encodeResponses (\n    65\t    config:EncodeConfig,\n    66\t    req:EncodeRequest\n    67\t):Record<string, unknown> {\n    68\t    const body:Record<string, unknown> = {\n    69\t        model:config.model,\n    70\t        input:input(config.model, req),\n    71\t        max_output_tokens:config.maxOutputTokens,\n    72\t        store:false,\n    73\t        stream:true,\n    74\t    }\n    75\t    if (req.tools.length > 0) {\n    76\t        body.tools = req.tools.map(tool => ({\n    77\t            type:'function',\n    78\t            name:tool.name,\n    79\t            description:tool.description ?? '',\n    80\t            parameters:structuredClone(tool.schema),\n    81\t            strict:false,\n    82\t        }))\n    83\t        body.tool_choice = 'auto'\n    84\t    }\n    85\t    return body\n    86\t}\n    87\t\n    88\ttype Json = Record<string, unknown>\n    89\t\n    90\tfunction obj (v:unknown):Json {\n    91\t    return v !== null && typeof v === 'object' && !Array.isArray(v) ?\n    92\t        v as Json :\n    93\t        {}\n    94\t}\n    95\t\n    96\tfunction str (v:unknown):string {\n    97\t    return typeof v === 'string' ? wellFormed(v) : ''\n    98\t}\n    99\t\n   100\tfunction codeOf (v:unknown):string {\n   101\t    return typeof v === 'number' ? String(v) : str(v)\n   102\t}\n   103\t\n   104\tfunction failed (prefix:string, message:string, code:string):ProviderError {\n   105\t    const suffix = code !== '' ? ` (code: ${code})` : ''\n   106\t    return new ProviderError(`${prefix}: ${message}${suffix}`, {\n   107\t        providerCode:code || undefined,\n   108\t        providerMessage:message,\n   109\t        retryable:false,\n   110\t    })\n   111\t}\n   112\t\n   113\tfunction finishFor (reason:string, hasCall:boolean):FinishReason {\n   114\t    if (reason === '') return hasCall ? 'tool-calls' : 'stop'\n   115\t    if (reason === 'max_tokens' || reason === 'max_output_tokens') {\n   116\t        return 'length'\n   117\t    }\n   118\t    if (reason === 'content_filter') return 'content-filter'\n   119\t    return hasCall ? 'tool-calls' : 'other'\n   120\t}\n   121\t\n   122\t// Assembles one turn from Responses API events (spec 06, 2.8.2). Reads\n   123\t// the stream to its end so capture sees every byte; events after the\n   124\t// terminal one are ignored.\n   125\texport async function decodeResponses (\n   126\t    events:AsyncIterable<SseEvent>\n   127\t):Promise<ModelTurn> {\n   128\t    const parts:AssistantPart[] = []\n   129\t    const open = new Set<number>()\n   130\t    let last:AssistantPart|null = null\n   131\t    let hasCall = false\n   132\t    let terminal:Json|null = null\n   133\t\n   134\t    function append (type:'text'|'reasoning', delta:string):void {\n   135\t        if (last && last.type !== 'tool-call' && last.type === type) {\n   136\t            last.text += delta\n   137\t            return\n   138\t        }\n   139\t        const part = { type, text:delta }\n   140\t        last = part\n   141\t        parts.push(part)\n   142\t    }\n   143\t\n   144\t    for await (const ev of events) {\n   145\t        if (terminal) continue\n   146\t        let data:Json\n   147\t        try {\n   148\t            data = obj(JSON.parse(ev.data))\n   149\t        } catch (err) {\n   150\t            throw new ProviderError('malformed responses stream event',\n   151\t                { retryable:false, cause:err })\n   152\t        }\n   153\t        const type = str(data.type) || ev.event\n   154\t        const index = typeof data.output_index === 'number' ?\n   155\t            data.output_index :\n   156\t            0\n   157\t        const item = obj(data.item)\n   158\t        switch (type) {\n   159\t            case 'response.output_item.added':\n   160\t                if (item.type === 'function_call') open.add(index)\n   161\t                break\n   162\t            case 'response.output_item.done':\n   163\t                if (item.type === 'function_call' && open.has(index)) {\n   164\t                    open.delete(index)\n   165\t                    last = {\n   166\t                        type:'tool-call',\n   167\t                        id:str(item.call_id),\n   168\t                        name:str(item.name),\n   169\t                        input:str(item.arguments),\n   170\t                    }\n   171\t                    parts.push(last)\n   172\t                    hasCall = true\n   173\t                }\n   174\t                break\n   175\t            case 'response.output_text.delta':\n   176\t                append('text', str(data.delta))\n   177\t                break\n   178\t            case 'response.reasoning_summary_text.delta':\n   179\t                append('reasoning', str(data.delta))\n   180\t                break\n   181\t            case 'response.completed':\n   182\t            case 'response.incomplete':\n   183\t                terminal = obj(data.response)\n   184\t                break\n   185\t            case 'response.failed': {\n   186\t                const e = obj(obj(data.response).error)\n   187\t                throw failed('response failed', str(e.message),\n   188\t                    codeOf(e.code))\n   189\t            }\n   190\t            case 'error':\n   191\t                throw failed('response error', str(data.message),\n   192\t                    codeOf(data.code))\n   193\t            default:\n   194\t                break\n   195\t        }\n   196\t    }\n   197\t    if (!terminal) throw new IncompleteStreamError()\n   198\t\n   199\t    const reason = str(obj(terminal.incomplete_details).reason)\n   200\t    const turn:ModelTurn = {\n   201\t        parts,\n   202\t        finishReason:finishFor(reason, hasCall),\n   203\t        usage:normalizeUsage(responsesUsage(terminal.usage)),\n   204\t    }\n   205\t    if (reason !== '') turn.rawFinishReason = reason\n   206\t    return turn\n   207\t}\n     1\t// `createModelClient` and `send` (spec 06, 3.2): one model turn becomes\n     2\t// exactly one HTTP request in the profile's protocol. Never retries.\n     3\t\n     4\timport { goTrimSpace } from '../gocompat/strings.js'\n     5\timport {\n     6\t    anthropicUrl,\n     7\t    decodeAnthropic,\n     8\t    encodeAnthropic,\n     9\t} from './anthropic.js'\n    10\timport { abortable, CaptureGate, openCapturedBody } from './capture.js'\n    11\timport { chatUrl, decodeChat, encodeChat } from './chat.js'\n    12\timport {\n    13\t    CaptureError,\n    14\t    EndpointError,\n    15\t    ProviderError,\n    16\t    SENTINEL_MESSAGE,\n    17\t} from './errors.js'\n    18\timport { currentFetch, requestHeaders } from './http.js'\n    19\timport {\n    20\t    decodeResponses,\n    21\t    encodeResponses,\n    22\t    responsesUrl,\n    23\t} from './responses.js'\n    24\timport { parseSse, type SseEvent } from './sse.js'\n    25\timport {\n    26\t    DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS,\n    27\t    runConversation,\n    28\t    type LoopDeps,\n    29\t} from './agent.js'\n    30\timport type { Ledger } from './ledger.js'\n    31\timport type { Sleep } from './retry.js'\n    32\timport type {\n    33\t    Client,\n    34\t    ClientConfig,\n    35\t    ModelRequest,\n    36\t    ModelTurn,\n    37\t    Protocol,\n    38\t    RecordUsage,\n    39\t    Usage,\n    40\t} from './types.js'\n    41\timport { UsageAccumulator } from './usage.js'\n    42\t\n    43\texport { DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS }\n    44\t\n    45\t// Error bodies are read at most this far (deliberate change 9).\n    46\texport const MAX_ERROR_BODY = 32 * 1024\n    47\t\n    48\texport interface ModelClient {\n    49\t    readonly config:Readonly<ClientConfig>;\n    50\t    // '' normalized to 'chat'.\n    51\t    readonly protocol:Protocol;\n    52\t    // <= 0 normalized to DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS.\n    53\t    readonly maxAttempts:number;\n    54\t    // One HTTP attempt. Resolves only after capture succeeded.\n    55\t    send (request:ModelRequest):Promise<ModelTurn>;\n    56\t    // Exact byte length of the request body `send` would post.\n    57\t    requestBytes (request:ModelRequest):number;\n    58\t    // Accumulated usage across all calls on this client.\n    59\t    usage ():Usage;\n    60\t}\n    61\t\n    62\tinterface Adapter {\n    63\t    url (baseUrl:string):string;\n    64\t    encode (config:ClientConfig, request:ModelRequest):unknown;\n    65\t    decode (events:AsyncIterable<SseEvent>):Promise<ModelTurn>;\n    66\t}\n    67\t\n    68\tconst ADAPTERS:Partial<Record<Protocol, Adapter>> = {\n    69\t    chat:{\n    70\t        url:chatUrl,\n    71\t        encode:(config, request) => encodeChat(config, request),\n    72\t        decode:decodeChat,\n    73\t    },\n    74\t    responses:{\n    75\t        url:responsesUrl,\n    76\t        encode:(config, request) => encodeResponses(config, request),\n    77\t        decode:decodeResponses,\n    78\t    },\n    79\t    anthropic:{\n    80\t        url:anthropicUrl,\n    81\t        encode:(config, request) => encodeAnthropic(config, request),\n    82\t        decode:decodeAnthropic,\n    83\t    },\n    84\t}\n    85\t\n    86\tfunction adapterFor (protocol:string):Adapter {\n    87\t    const known = protocol === 'chat' || protocol === 'responses' ||\n    88\t        protocol === 'anthropic'\n    89\t    const adapter = known ? ADAPTERS[protocol as Protocol] : undefined\n    90\t    if (!adapter) {\n    91\t        throw new Error(`unsupported inference protocol \"${protocol}\"`)\n    92\t    }\n    93\t    return adapter\n    94\t}\n    95\t\n    96\t// Best-effort provider error fields from an OpenAI-style\n    97\t// `{\"error\":{...}}` or Anthropic `{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{...}}` body.\n    98\tfunction providerFields (text:string):{\n    99\t    type?:string;\n   100\t    code?:string;\n   101\t    message?:string;\n   102\t} {\n   103\t    try {\n   104\t        const parsed:unknown = JSON.parse(text)\n   105\t        if (parsed === null || typeof parsed !== 'object') return {}\n   106\t        const e = (parsed as { error?:unknown }).error\n   107\t        if (e === null || typeof e !== 'object') return {}\n   108\t        const { type, code, message } = e as Record<string, unknown>\n   109\t        return {\n   110\t            type:typeof type === 'string' ? type : undefined,\n   111\t            code:typeof code === 'string' ?\n   112\t                code :\n   113\t                typeof code === 'number' ? String(code) : undefined,\n   114\t            message:typeof message === 'string' ? message : undefined,\n   115\t        }\n   116\t    } catch {\n   117\t        return {}\n   118\t    }\n   119\t}\n   120\t\n   121\tasync function readCapped (\n   122\t    body:ReadableStream<Uint8Array>|null,\n   123\t    limit:number,\n   124\t    signal:AbortSignal\n   125\t):Promise<Uint8Array> {\n   126\t    if (!body) return new Uint8Array(0)\n   127\t    const reader = body.getReader()\n   128\t    const parts:Uint8Array[] = []\n   129\t    let size = 0\n   130\t    let eof = false\n   131\t    try {\n   132\t        while (size < limit) {\n   133\t            const r = await abortable(reader.read(), signal)\n   134\t            if (r.done) {\n   135\t                eof = true\n   136\t                break\n   137\t            }\n   138\t            const take = r.value.subarray(0, limit - size)\n   139\t            parts.push(take)\n   140\t            size += take.length\n   141\t        }\n   142\t    } finally {\n   143\t        if (!eof) await reader.cancel().catch(() => {})\n   144\t    }\n   145\t    const out = new Uint8Array(size)\n   146\t    let off = 0\n   147\t    for (const p of parts) {\n   148\t        out.set(p, off)\n   149\t        off += p.length\n   150\t    }\n   151\t    return out\n   152\t}\n   153\t\n   154\tasync function httpError (\n   155\t    response:Response,\n   156\t    url:string,\n   157\t    model:string,\n   158\t    signal:AbortSignal\n   159\t):Promise<Error> {\n   160\t    const bytes = await readCapped(response.body, MAX_ERROR_BODY, signal)\n   161\t    const text = new TextDecoder().decode(bytes)\n   162\t    const fields = providerFields(text)\n   163\t    const headers:Record<string, string> = {}\n   164\t    response.headers.forEach((value, name) => { headers[name] = value })\n   165\t    const detail = fields.message ?? text.slice(0, 512).trim()\n   166\t    const status = `${response.status} ${response.statusText}`.trim()\n   167\t    const err = new ProviderError(\n   168\t        `POST \"${url}\": ${status}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`,\n   169\t        {\n   170\t            status:response.status,\n   171\t            headers,\n   172\t            providerType:fields.type,\n   173\t            providerCode:fields.code,\n   174\t            providerMessage:fields.message,\n   175\t        })\n   176\t    if (response.status >= 300 && response.status < 400) {\n   177\t        return new EndpointError(\n   178\t            `${SENTINEL_MESSAGE.endpoint}: ${model}: redirect refused: ` +\n   179\t                err.message,\n   180\t            { cause:err, details:{ model } })\n   181\t    }\n   182\t    return err\n   183\t}\n   184\t\n   185\texport function createModelClient (config:ClientConfig):ModelClient {\n   186\t    if (!(config.maxOutputTokens > 0)) {\n   187\t        throw new Error(`${config.model}: max output tokens must be positive`)\n   188\t    }\n   189\t    if (goTrimSpace(config.apiKey) === '') {\n   190\t        throw new Error(`${config.model}: API key is not configured`)\n   191\t    }\n   192\t    const protocol = (config.protocol === '' ?\n   193\t        'chat' :\n   194\t        config.protocol) as Protocol\n   195\t    const adapter = adapterFor(protocol)\n   196\t    const maxAttempts = config.maxAttempts > 0 ?\n   197\t        config.maxAttempts :\n   198\t        DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS\n   199\t    const gate = new CaptureGate()\n   200\t    const total = new UsageAccumulator()\n   201\t    const url = adapter.url(config.baseUrl)\n   202\t\n   203\t    function encodeBody (request:ModelRequest):Uint8Array {\n   204\t        const body = adapter.encode(config, request)\n   205\t        return new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(body))\n   206\t    }\n   207\t\n   208\t    async function attempt (\n   209\t        request:ModelRequest,\n   210\t        signal:AbortSignal\n   211\t    ):Promise<ModelTurn> {\n   212\t        const fetchFn = config.fetch ?? currentFetch()\n   213\t        const response = await fetchFn(url, {\n   214\t            method:'POST',\n   215\t            headers:requestHeaders(protocol, config.apiKey,\n   216\t                request.sessionId, config.sessionHeader),\n   217\t            body:encodeBody(request),\n   218\t            redirect:'manual',\n   219\t            signal,\n   220\t        })\n   221\t        if (response.status < 200 || response.status >= 300) {\n   222\t            throw await httpError(response, url, config.model, signal)\n   223\t        }\n   224\t        const body = await openCapturedBody(response, {\n   225\t            role:config.role,\n   226\t            protocol,\n   227\t            model:config.model,\n   228\t            captureResponse:config.captureResponse,\n   229\t        }, gate, signal)\n   230\t        let turn:ModelTurn|undefined\n   231\t        let failure:unknown\n   232\t        try {\n   233\t            turn = await adapter.decode(parseSse(body.chunks))\n   234\t        } catch (err) {\n   235\t            failure = err\n   236\t        }\n   237\t        if (turn) {\n   238\t            total.add(turn.usage)\n   239\t            request.onUsage?.(turn.usage)\n   240\t        }\n   241\t        // A capture failure here replaces any turn or error.\n   242\t        await body.release()\n   243\t        if (!turn) throw failure\n   244\t        signal.throwIfAborted()\n   245\t        return turn\n   246\t    }\n   247\t\n   248\t    return {\n   249\t        config,\n   250\t        protocol,\n   251\t        maxAttempts,\n   252\t        requestBytes (request:ModelRequest):number {\n   253\t            return encodeBody(request).length\n   254\t        },\n   255\t        usage ():Usage {\n   256\t            return total.total()\n   257\t        },\n   258\t        async send (request:ModelRequest):Promise<ModelTurn> {\n   259\t            if (gate.failure) throw gate.failure\n   260\t            request.signal.throwIfAborted()\n   261\t            const timeout = config.requestTimeoutMs > 0 ?\n   262\t                AbortSignal.timeout(config.requestTimeoutMs) :\n   263\t                undefined\n   264\t            const signal = timeout ?\n   265\t                AbortSignal.any([request.signal, timeout]) :\n   266\t                request.signal\n   267\t            try {\n   268\t                return await attempt(request, signal)\n   269\t            } catch (err) {\n   270\t                if (err instanceof CaptureError) throw err\n   271\t                if (request.signal.aborted) throw request.signal.reason\n   272\t                if (timeout?.aborted) {\n   273\t                    throw new EndpointError(\n   274\t                        `${SENTINEL_MESSAGE.endpoint}: ${config.model}: ` +\n   275\t                            'request timed out after ' +\n   276\t                            `${config.requestTimeoutMs}ms`,\n   277\t                        {\n   278\t                            cause:timeout.reason,\n   279\t                            details:{ model:config.model },\n   280\t                        })\n   281\t                }\n   282\t                throw err\n   283\t            }\n   284\t        },\n   285\t    }\n   286\t}\n   287\t\n   288\texport interface CreateClientOptions {\n   289\t    // The run's shared ledger; none means unlimited.\n   290\t    ledger?:Ledger|null;\n   291\t    now?:() => number;\n   292\t    sleep?:Sleep;\n   293\t    sessionId?:() => string;\n   294\t}\n   295\t\n   296\tfunction recordUsage (u:Usage):RecordUsage {\n   297\t    return {\n   298\t        uncached_input_tokens:u.uncachedInputTokens,\n   299\t        cached_input_tokens:u.cachedInputTokens,\n   300\t        cache_write_tokens:u.cacheWriteTokens,\n   301\t        output_tokens:u.outputTokens,\n   302\t        calls:u.calls,\n   303\t    }\n   304\t}\n   305\t\n   306\t// The `Client` the finder and verifier call (spec 07, 3.3): both entry\n   307\t// points run the agent loop over `model`; usage accumulates across all\n   308\t// of this client's conversations.\n   309\texport function createClient (\n   310\t    model:ModelClient,\n   311\t    opts:CreateClientOptions = {}\n   312\t):Client {\n   313\t    const total = new UsageAccumulator()\n   314\t    const deps:LoopDeps = {\n   315\t        client:model,\n   316\t        model:model.config.model,\n   317\t        maxOutputTokens:model.config.maxOutputTokens,\n   318\t        maxAttempts:model.maxAttempts > 0 ?\n   319\t            model.maxAttempts :\n   320\t            DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS,\n   321\t        ledger:opts.ledger ?? null,\n   322\t        addUsage:u => total.add(u),\n   323\t        now:opts.now,\n   324\t        sleep:opts.sleep,\n   325\t        sessionId:opts.sessionId,\n   326\t    }\n   327\t    return {\n   328\t        name:model.config.model,\n   329\t        converse (system, user, converseOpts, signal) {\n   330\t            return runConversation(deps, system, user, converseOpts, false,\n   331\t                signal)\n   332\t        },\n   333\t        completeStructured (system, user, schemaName, result, signal) {\n   334\t            return runConversation(deps, system, user, {\n   335\t                tools:[{\n   336\t                    name:schemaName,\n   337\t                    description:'Return the requested structured result.',\n   338\t                    schema:result.schema,\n   339\t                }],\n   340\t                finalTool:schemaName,\n   341\t                final:{ decode:result.decode },\n   342\t                maxTurns:1,\n   343\t            }, true, signal)\n   344\t        },\n   345\t        usage () {\n   346\t            return recordUsage(total.total())\n   347\t        },\n   348\t    }\n   349\t}\n     1\t# LLM layer and agent loop (TS)\n     2\t\n     3\t`src/llm/`.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Adapters\n     6\t\n     7\t- Adapters read no environment variable. A protocol is an entry in\n     8\t  `ADAPTERS` (`client.ts`) with a pure encoder and an\n     9\t  `AsyncIterable<SseEvent>` decoder returning a `ModelTurn`; `send` owns\n    10\t  fetch, headers (`http.ts` `requestHeaders`), capture, usage, and\n    11\t  abort.\n    12\t- One `errors.ts`: `LlmError.kind` (underscore names, read by\n    13\t  `src/cli/errors.ts`) and `sentinels` (hyphen names, `hasSentinel`)\n    14\t  must stay in step.\n    15\t- Tool results sent to models go through `encodeToolResult` (`json.ts`)\n    16\t  only.\n    17\t- `anthropic` (`anthropic.ts`) groups items into alternating role\n    18\t  messages first, then drops a thinking-only assistant message; it never\n    19\t  edits, reorders, or drops a signed block. `tool_choice` matches Go\n    20\t  (`{type: auto, disable_parallel_tool_use: false}`).\n    21\t- Usage stage 1 lives in `usage.ts` per protocol (`chatUsage`,\n    22\t  `responsesUsage`, `anthropicUsage`); decoders call `normalizeUsage`\n    23\t  on its result.\n    24\t- Making an adapter available changes tests that pin unavailability:\n    25\t  the construction test in `test/llm/client.ts` and the doctor roundtrip\n    26\t  test (`test/cli/doctor.ts`, whose `doctorProbe` must speak the\n    27\t  protocol).\n    28\t\n    29\t## Agent loop (`agent.ts`, `runConversation`)\n    30\t\n    31\t- `createClient(modelClient, {ledger, now, sleep, sessionId})`\n    32\t  (`client.ts`) wraps a `ModelClient` into the finder/verifier `Client`.\n    33\t  The pure decision is `reviewResponse` (`review.ts`); the deadline,\n    34\t  ledger, final-argument validation, and retries are separate modules.\n    35\t- `ModelClient.send` owns the request timeout; the loop composes only\n    36\t  caller + deadline/window signals.\n    37\t- Cutoff errors come from `cutoffError` (`errors.ts`), which keeps the\n    38\t  cause out of the matchable chain; tests assert `details.stopCause`\n    39\t  kinds, never message text.\n    40\t\n    41\t## Tests\n    42\t\n    43\t- `test/helpers/inference-server.ts` (`startInferenceServer`: a script\n    44\t  picks a reply per request; it records method, path, headers, raw and\n    45\t  parsed body) and `inference-stream.ts` (`writeInferenceStream`, the\n    46\t  native SSE per protocol). The `responses` writer, like Go's, emits\n    47\t  every output item as a function call, so message items yield no text.\n    48\t- `test/helpers/anthropic-fakes.ts`: `anthropicCalls` (a Messages\n    49\t  response), `startBindingServer` (rejects a signed thinking block whose\n    50\t  prefix changed; counts `rejected`), and `deepSeekScript` /\n    51\t  `startDeepSeekServer` (400 on a forced tool choice or a missing\n    52\t  reasoning replay). `deepSeekScript` plugs into `settingsRepo`, whose\n    53\t  fetch rewrites every origin to its own server.\n    54\t- A fake that answers a different protocol than the request path makes\n    55\t  the client see an incomplete stream and retry with the 5 s backoff;\n    56\t  branch on `req.path` when one script serves two protocols.\n    57\t- CLI review tests on `responses` use `responsesProfileConfig`,\n    58\t  `responsesFindingsReply`, and `responsesCalls` (`test/helpers/review.ts`).\n    59\t  Requests through `runRoast`'s rewriting fetch carry\n    60\t  `transfer-encoding`; filter it with the other transport headers.\n    61\t- Byte-level body behavior (read-ahead, caps, cancel counts) is tested\n    62\t  with a `highWaterMark: 0` `ReadableStream` returned through\n    63\t  `ClientConfig.fetch`; `new Response(stream)` neither copies nor\n    64\t  pre-reads it.\n    65\t- Agent-loop tests drive `harness(script)` from\n    66\t  `test/llm/agent-helpers.ts` (a scripted fake `ModelClient`: canned\n    67\t  turns, errors, or functions of the request; sleeps recorded).\n    68\t- `AbortSignal.timeout` timers do not keep Node alive, so a fake step\n    69\t  that waits for an abort must hold a timer (the `aborted()` helper\n    70\t  does); otherwise the test process just exits.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01T6H39Mzrb9HTVEpUPxaMw9","agent_id":"a2d564e3db2c159ee","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","uuid":"1701e690-775f-4226-8d88-4c4122c8ace9","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:03:55.010Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JZhEWkt1U7UBcSbeSkRHGx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose","task_description":"Review LLM adapters"}
