{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ANB5dZiQtuBPUTLZDQao8A","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# 06 -- LLM protocol adapters\n11:## 1. Purpose\n34:## 2. Behavior contract\n36:### 2.1 Client construction\n69:### 2.2 Endpoint URL\n90:### 2.3 Request headers\n123:### 2.4 Ambient environment never influences requests\n147:### 2.5 Redirects\n156:### 2.6 Request bodies\n177:#### 2.6.1 `chat` (OpenAI Chat Completions; OpenRouter, DeepSeek, others)\n236:#### 2.6.2 `responses` (OpenAI Responses API; OpenRouter)\n274:#### 2.6.3 `anthropic` (native Messages API)\n335:### 2.7 SSE parsing (shared)\n366:### 2.8 Turn assembly\n374:#### 2.8.1 `chat` chunks\n418:#### 2.8.2 `responses` events\n452:#### 2.8.3 `anthropic` events\n484:#### 2.8.4 Decoding model output\n492:### 2.9 Usage normalization\n552:### 2.10 Errors and classification\n624:### 2.11 Raw response capture\n673:### 2.12 Request timeout and cancellation\n687:### 2.13 Provider quirks (summary)\n709:## 3. TypeScript module design\n735:### 3.1 Types (`types.ts`)\n817:### 3.2 Adapter interface consumed by the agent loop (`client.ts`)\n853:### 3.3 Obligations the agent loop keeps (cross-reference)\n868:### 3.4 Errors (`errors.ts`)\n901:### 3.5 Other modules\n936:## 4. Deliberate changes\n958:## 5. Test plan\n1097:## 6. Go baseline references\n1125:## 7. Resolved","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01T6H39Mzrb9HTVEpUPxaMw9","agent_id":"a2d564e3db2c159ee","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","uuid":"0a44b9a3-6f4c-49f5-98d8-a7572b008425","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:04:00.166Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ANB5dZiQtuBPUTLZDQao8A","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose","task_description":"Review LLM adapters"}
