{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DN78AyfxkZR5Y79BktaaXC","type":"tool_result","content":".scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/10-records.md:220:| `merge_base_oid` | omit when empty |\n.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/01-cli.md:405:    merge-base OID, head OID, survey, staged, files), derived meta (mode,\n.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/04-scope.md:213:   4. `rangeArgs = buildRangeArgs(resolvedBase)`: run `merge-base <base>\n.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/04-scope.md:473:   `baseOID`, `mergeBaseOID` empty.\n.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/04-scope.md:714:  `merge-base` probe).\n.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/04-scope.md:777:  scope, `includeWorktree`, `baseOID`, `mergeBaseOID`, `cUnquote`, or\nsrc/scope/build.ts:127:    if (await gitOk(repo, ['merge-base', base, 'HEAD'], opts)) {\n    scope?:string;\n    stagedTreeOID?:string;\n    maxFileDiffBytes?:number;\n    // The environment git runs with (the CLI context's env); process.env\n    // when absent. An ambient GIT_INDEX_FILE in it is honored.\n    env?:NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n}\n\nexport interface Scope {\n    readonly diff:string;\n    readonly diffBytes:Buffer;\n    readonly files:readonly string[];\n    readonly base:string;\n    readonly notes:readonly string[];\n    readonly staged:boolean;\n    readonly stagedTreeOID:string;\n    readonly manifest:string;\n    readonly survey:boolean;\n    readonly headOID:string;\n}\n\nexport interface SizeEntry {\n    path:string;\n    bytes:number;\n}\n\n// Whether there is nothing to review.\nexport function isEmpty (scope:Scope):boolean {\n    if (scope.survey) return scope.files.length === 0\n    return goTrimSpace(scope.diff) === ''\n}\n\nfunction makeScope (diffBytes:Buffer, fields:Partial<Scope>):Scope {\n    return {\n        diff:diffBytes.toString('utf8'),\n        diffBytes,\n        files:[],\n        base:'',\n        notes:[],\n        staged:false,\n        stagedTreeOID:'',\n        manifest:'',\n        survey:false,\n        headOID:'',\n        ...fields,\n    }\n}\n\n// The pathspec arguments: none at all when every list is empty.\nexport function pathspecArgs (\n    paths:readonly string[],\n    excludes:readonly string[],\n    literalExcludes:readonly string[]\n):string[] {\n    if (paths.length === 0 && excludes.length === 0 &&\n        literalExcludes.length === 0) {\n        return []\n    }\n    return [\n        '--',\n        ...paths,\n        ...excludes.map(p => `:(exclude)${p}`),\n        ...literalExcludes.map(p => `:(exclude,literal)${p}`),\n    ]\n}\n\n// The first candidate ref that resolves, or ''.\nexport async function resolveBase (\n    repo:string,\n    requested:string,\n    opts:GitRunOpts\n):Promise<string> {\n    const candidates = requested ? [requested] : BASE_CANDIDATES\n    for (const ref of candidates) {\n        if (await gitOk(repo, ['rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', ref],\n            opts)) {\n            return ref\n        }\n    }\n    return ''\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018gF4SKTMT76p6W4DKSyVyJ","agent_id":"a65d44a24feed96f9","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","uuid":"63f616fe-f36f-491a-a3af-6a8d25ce586d","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:04:36.191Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DN78AyfxkZR5Y79BktaaXC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose","task_description":"Review review cmd/verify/gate"}
