{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0145yRPbjm5vrvmZELS59dZo","type":"tool_result","content":"   HEAD: <q(headLine)>            (or \"HEAD: (no commits)\" when empty)\n   <F> tracked file(s) across <D> top-level director(ies)\n\n   ### Files by top-level directory ###\n   <q(dir)> (<count>)             (one per directory)\n\n   ### Tracked files ###\n   <q(file)>                      (one per file)\n   ```\n   Every line ends in `\\n`. If any `q` call quoted, append\n   `\\n(Names in double quotes contain control or markup characters and\n   are Go-escaped; unescape one before passing it to a tool.)\\n`.\n7. Return `{manifest, survey:true, files, headOID, notes}`; `base`,\n   `baseOID`, `mergeBaseOID` empty.\n\n#### 2.12.1 manifestQuote\n\nA name is safe (returned unchanged) when it contains none\nof `\"`, `\\`, `<`, `>`, and every code point is printable per Go's\n`unicode.IsPrint`: categories L, M, N, P, S, plus U+0020 only (other\nspaces, controls, format characters, line/paragraph separators are not).\nOtherwise return Go `strconv.Quote(s)` with every `<` replaced by `\\x3c`\nand every `>` by `\\x3e`. `strconv.Quote` rules: wrap in `\"`; `\"` and `\\`\nescaped with `\\`; printable code points literal; `\\a \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t \\v`\nfor those controls; other code points below U+0020 and U+007F as `\\xNN`;\nother non-printable code points as\n`\\uXXXX` (< U+10000) or `\\UXXXXXXXX`. Hex digits are lowercase. Names\nreaching it are always valid UTF-8 (2.15), so Go's invalid-byte `\\xNN`\ncase does not arise. Unicode printable differences between Go's\n`unicode.IsPrint` and JS `\\p{...}` classes for newly assigned code points\nare accepted (deliberate change, section 4).\n  package had no context). Aborting kills the running git child and\n  rejects with an `AbortError`; best-effort steps do not swallow it.\n- Windows is unsupported, so `/dev/null` is used literally for\n  `core.attributesFile` (Go used `os.DevNull`).\n- `fit` returns a new Scope instead of mutating in place (no observable\n  difference: the CLI already used the pre-fit diff for grounding).\n- Branch survey scope is not ported (deliberate change 23): no `branch`\n  scope, `includeWorktree`, `baseOID`, `mergeBaseOID`, `cUnquote`, or\n  branch tests.\n- Name lists and `ls-files --others` use `-z` (deliberate change 15).\n- Names that are not valid UTF-8 are skipped with a warning note\n  (deliberate change 24); git output is read as `Buffer`, and `Scope`\n  carries `diffBytes` so hashed or recorded diff bytes are exact.\n- The `fit` breakdown uses a stable sort (deliberate change 18).\n- Staged linguist exclusion lists a rename's deleted side too, via\n  `--no-renames` (deliberate change 16).\n    8_000_000`. If UTF-8 bytes of finder system + finder user >\n    ceiling: `UsageError` `finder prompt is <n> bytes, over the <c>-byte\n    ceiling; narrow the review scope or adjust limits.max_diff_bytes,\n    limits.max_file_ctx_bytes, or limits.max_prompt_bytes in the project\n    config`. No request is sent and the snapshot is deleted.\n15. **Run record init.** Build meta (records area owns the shape):\n    run ID, UTC timestamp (RFC 3339 with nanoseconds in Go; see records\n    area), repo, argv (the argv given to `run`, without the program\n    name), roast `{version, commit}`, scope meta (kind, base, uncommitted\n    only, staged only, include vendored, paths, excludes, base OID,\n    merge-base OID, head OID, survey, staged, files), derived meta (mode,\n    langs, quick, interactive, max turns, confidence floor, do verify,\n    task, max severity as typed, max diff bytes, max file ctx bytes),\n    roles meta for `finder` and `verifier` (profile, base URL, model,\n    protocol, max output tokens, session header, digest of that role's\n    system prompt), snapshot meta, digests (input kind, digest and byte\n    length of the reviewed input, digests of system and user prompts),\n    budgets, env names only (records `CaptureEnv` over\n    `cfg.CredentialEnvNames()`), caveats from the snapshot. Scope base and\n    head OIDs fall back to the snapshot meta's base/head when the scope\n    has none. Then write meta (required) and the artifacts `input`,\n    `finder_system`, `finder_user`, `verifier_system` (required). Any\n    failure: remove the run directory and return\n    `initialize run record: <e>` or `initialize run artifact <name>: <e>`\n    (exit 4; the snapshot is deleted). After success the snapshot is\n    durable and is kept on every later exit.\n\t\tnotes = append(notes, \"IncludeWorktree set: dirty-tree guard bypassed, but worktree changes are NOT included anywhere — the manifest, Files, and OIDs below describe committed HEAD only\")\n\t}\n\n\tbaseOID, err := gitOut(repo, \"rev-parse\", base)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn Scope{}, fmt.Errorf(\"git rev-parse %s: %w\", base, err)\n\t}\n\tbaseOID = strings.TrimSpace(baseOID)\n\theadOID, err := gitOut(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn Scope{}, fmt.Errorf(\"git rev-parse HEAD: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\theadOID = strings.TrimSpace(headOID)\n\tmergeBaseOID, err := gitOut(repo, \"merge-base\", baseOID, headOID)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn Scope{}, fmt.Errorf(\"no merge base between %s and HEAD; the histories are unrelated\", base)\n\t}\n\tmergeBaseOID = strings.TrimSpace(mergeBaseOID)\n\n\tdiffFlags := append([]string{\"--no-renames\"}, PatchFlags...)\n\t// Pin the range to the captured headOID, not the mutable \"HEAD\" ref: a\n\t// concurrent commit/checkout between the rev-parse above and these git\n\t// invocations would otherwise make the manifest describe a different\n\t// commit than the returned HeadOID, defeating the immutable-snapshot\n\t// guarantee documented on Scope.\n\trangeSpec := mergeBaseOID + \"..\" + headOID\n\n\tstatArgs := append([]string{\"diff\"}, diffFlags...)\n\tstatArgs = append(statArgs, \"--stat\", rangeSpec)\n\tstatArgs = append(statArgs, spec...)\n\tstat, err := gitOut(repo, statArgs...)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018gF4SKTMT76p6W4DKSyVyJ","agent_id":"a65d44a24feed96f9","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","uuid":"b9995218-111f-4246-a002-bc70e7434839","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:04:38.119Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0145yRPbjm5vrvmZELS59dZo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose","task_description":"Review review cmd/verify/gate"}
