{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01By7N8kf1MPXGCNX8B268Yx","type":"tool_result","content":"2:# roast-gate-hook: v1\n3:# Managed by `roast gate` — this file is regenerated on refresh, so local\n4:# edits are lost. To stop the gate in this repo: `roast gate disable`.\n9:# `roast review --staged` sees that path's content and nothing else. Never\n12:# Fails the commit ONLY when roast exits 1 (a finding at or above the\n13:# threshold). Every infrastructure failure — no roast binary, no inference\n14:# credentials, endpoint unreachable, timeout, empty stdout (which means the review never\n19:# Runs node_modules/.bin/roast at the Git toplevel (the project's npm\n20:# install), never a roast from PATH. The watchdog (gate.timeout_seconds,\n29:warn() { printf 'roast gate: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; }\n37:# enrollment: only this repository's local decision can authorize a review.\n39:decision=$(git config --local --get roast.gate 2>/dev/null |\n47:# Run the project-installed roast (`npm install --save-dev`), never one from\n49:toplevel=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null) || toplevel=\"\"\n50:ROAST=\"${toplevel:-.}/node_modules/.bin/roast\"\n52:  warn \"roast binary not found at node_modules/.bin/roast (run npm install); commit allowed WITHOUT review\"\n57:# be resolved against each git child's own directory rather than ours — roast\n61:# would review the wrong index.\n79:work=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR%/}/roast-gate.XXXXXX\") || {\n80:  warn \"could not create a temp dir; commit allowed WITHOUT review\"\n88:# `gate` section, read through the same binary that runs the review. A roast\n89:# that cannot report them (no project config, an invalid one) cannot review\n93:  warn \"could not read gate settings; commit allowed WITHOUT review\"\n109:warn \"reviewing the staged content of this commit (ROAST_SKIP=1 bypasses)...\"\n111:# stdout is roast's JSON result, stderr its markdown — captured, not streamed,\n113:# The child never offers to bootstrap a hook of its own: roast suppresses the\n115:\"$ROAST\" review --staged --quick --format both \\\n116:  --max-severity \"$severity\" \\\n117:  --task \"pre-commit gate\" >\"$out\" 2>\"$err\" &\n121:# The poll loop exits as soon as roast does, so no stray long `sleep` outlives\n122:# the hook. SIGTERM is advisory — roast handles it, but a wedged process might\n158:  warn \"review timed out after ${timeout_s}s; commit allowed WITHOUT review (raise gate.timeout_seconds in .roast.json)\"\n162:# Empty stdout means roast never emitted a result: it died, could not\n164:# clean review — say so explicitly rather than letting silence read as a pass.\n166:  warn \"review produced no result (exit $rc); commit allowed WITHOUT review\"\n181:    warn \"review failed (exit $rc); commit allowed WITHOUT review\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018gF4SKTMT76p6W4DKSyVyJ","agent_id":"a65d44a24feed96f9","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","uuid":"a3442b45-3602-40ff-99e0-1cfd58bf25fa","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:06:05.831Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01By7N8kf1MPXGCNX8B268Yx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose","task_description":"Review review cmd/verify/gate"}
