{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H9UQ6ee2jbQtnWz3S1BPRu","type":"tool_result","content":"123:func Validate(resp FindingsResponse, confidenceFloor float64, ground func(file, quote string) bool) *Result {\n124-\tresult := &Result{\n125-\t\tAssessment: resp.Assessment,\n126-\t\tFindings:   []Finding{},\n127-\t\tDropped:    []Finding{},\n128-\t\tNotes:      []string{},\n129-\t}\n130-\tfor _, wf := range resp.Findings {\n131-\t\tf := wf.ToFinding()\n132-\t\t// Providers do not all enforce the schema's severity enum. Rank()\n133-\t\t// treats anything unrecognized as INFO, so an unnormalized \"high\"\n134-\t\t// would pass a --max-severity HIGH gate; canonicalize it, and drop\n135-\t\t// what cannot be canonicalized rather than let it rank as INFO.\n11:    result:Omit<Result, 'notes'>&{ notes?:string[]|null };\n97:        notes:r.result.notes ?? null,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018gF4SKTMT76p6W4DKSyVyJ","agent_id":"a65d44a24feed96f9","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","uuid":"036183c0-3c05-4234-8ef6-59354d38d2ae","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:06:31.839Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01H9UQ6ee2jbQtnWz3S1BPRu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose","task_description":"Review review cmd/verify/gate"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM6LbxSxMQH6dPAimoxY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found three real problems, the first one a security regression. The rest of the reviewed code matches Go apart from the deliberate changes. I checked these by reading the code and running a few git commands. I didn't run the test suite. I couldn't reproduce finding 1 on this Mac because APFS refuses non-UTF-8 file names.\n\n1. **Secret files with non-UTF-8 names get past the denylist** (security, Linux only). In `src/snapshot/denylist.ts:51-57`, `denylistedUntracked` calls `decodePaths(out).paths`, which silently drops names that aren't valid UTF-8 (`src/scope/text.ts:45-54`).\n   - **Input:** an untracked, non-ignored file `\\xff.pem` (or `\\xffdir/.env`) on Linux.\n   - **What goes wrong:** the file never reaches `excluded`, so `writeWorktree` (`src/snapshot/snapshot.ts:165-174`) runs `git add -A -- .` without an exclude for it. The secret goes into the pinned worktree tree and the `refs/roast/snapshots/<id>` commit, and `excluded_paths` reports nothing.\n   - **Wider impact:** `grep_repo` searches the pinned tree with no exclusions of its own (`src/context/grep.ts:80-91`). In live mode it adds `--untracked` with only the decodable exclusions. Either way, the secret's contents can reach the model.\n   - **Change 24 doesn't cover this:** it is about skipping such names from review, not capturing them.\n   - **Go reference:** `git show c0b539fc:internal/snapshot/snapshot.go`, `denylisted()`. It splits the raw `ls-files -z` bytes and runs `matchesAny` on them, so `\\xff.pem` matches `*.pem` and is excluded.\n   - **Fix:** match the denylist on raw bytes, or put undecodable untracked names in the excluded set (pass the raw bytes back through the exclude pathspec).\n   - **Missing test:** none in `test/snapshot/denylist.ts` or `snapshot.ts`; it needs a Linux-only (skip on darwin) test with a non-UTF-8 `.pem` file.\n\n2. **`--end-of-options` passed to `git rev-parse`** (likely portability break). See `src/snapshot/snapshot.ts:267` (`verify`) and `:290` (`load`).\n   - **Input:** any machine whose git predates `rev-parse` support for `--end-of-options`. I believe that arrived around git 2.43 (late 2023), but I couldn't confirm the exact version: only git 2.49 and 2.50 are installed here, and both accept it.\n   - **What goes wrong:** older `rev-parse` treats the token as an unknown flag, and with `--verify` it exits non-zero. `verify` swallows that and returns `''`. Then `headOid`, `revOid` and `treeOid` all return `''`, so every capture fails with \"repository has no commits\". `load` fails with \"no snapshot ref\", so `runs checkout` breaks too. That would hit Debian 12 (2.39) and Ubuntu 22.04 (2.34).\n   - **Go reference:** Go's `RevOID`, `TreeOID` and `Load` call `rev-parse --verify --quiet <rev>` without the token. Neither the spec nor the deliberate-change list mentions it.\n   - **Fix:** remove the token. The revs are always built internally (`<x>^{commit}`, `refs/roast/snapshots/...`), so it buys nothing.\n\n3. **`runs checkout` error messages for a missing or corrupt `meta.json` differ from Go** (minor parity break). `src/record/meta.ts:62-69` (`readMeta`, called from `src/cli/runs.ts:210`) passes the raw error through.\n   - **Missing file:** TS prints `ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '.../meta.json'`. Go prints `run <dir> has no meta.json: open ...: no such file or directory`.\n   - **Corrupt file:** TS prints a bare `expected an object` with no path. Go prints `parse <path>: <err>`.\n   - **Go reference:** `git show c0b539fc:internal/record/meta.go`, `ReadMeta` (lines 198-213).\n   - The exit code (2, usage error) is the same; only the message differs.\n\nOne low-priority hardening gap that matches Go, so it isn't a regression: `checkoutHandler` uses `meta.run_id` from inside `meta.json` without checking it, for the ref name and the default destination `tmpdir/<run_id>` (`src/cli/runs.ts:216-228`). Only the run ID typed on the command line is checked as a plain name (change 11). A hand-edited `run_id` of `../..` would move the default destination out of the temp dir. Git's ref-name rules stop `load` from turning that into a ref path problem.\n\nEverything else I compared matches Go or is covered by a deliberate change:\n- **Capture and pin:** composite tree, parents, identity, live-index resolution, literal excludes.\n- **Restore:** stripping `GIT_INDEX_FILE` and resolving the target dir once against cwd (change 12), and cleanup after a failed `worktree add`.\n- **`removeWorktree`.**\n- **Prune:** threshold and default, fractional milliseconds, skipping non-commits, stopping at the first delete error, hour rounding.\n- **`runs` list:** glob, sort, limit, `--json`, padding, CRLF handling, the 16 MiB line cap, `null` lines.\n- **`runs show`:** ID checks and exit code.\n- **Survey manifest:** quoting and the dirty-tree and linguist notes.\n- **`pinIndexTree`.**\n\nTest coverage looks adequate apart from the missing non-UTF-8 denylist test in finding 1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1057,"cache_read_input_tokens":104363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1057,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tw6eUvmTfMfsVNapeDwjUZ","agent_id":"acf0b2540a7701a5f","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","uuid":"f31355a2-013e-46a8-87bb-97740212700a","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:06:33.282Z","request_id":"req_011ChM6LbgKYz937LnxyeJ4f","subagent_type":"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose","task_description":"Review snapshot/runs/survey"}
