{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM6QZcASazBqvb2KAQvu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found no correctness bugs or parity breaks against Go in the reviewed files. Two low-severity items are worth noting: one contract slip against AGENTS.md and one test gap.\n\n**What matches Go:**\n- **Byte-identical files:** all 12 `src/prompts/templates/*.tmpl` files match `internal/prompts/templates/` under `cmp`. So do `src/gate/pre-commit.sh` vs `internal/gate/pre-commit.sh` and `src/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md` vs `internal/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`.\n- **User-message rendering:** `renderFinderUser` and `renderVerifierUser` in `src/prompts/render.ts` rebuild the Go templates by hand. The output matches, including the blank lines after `{{.Task}}`, the trailing `\\n\\n` and `\\n`, and `%.2f` confidence.\n- **Review order** (`src/cli/review.ts:228-586` vs `cli.go runReviewCommand`): flag validation, config, roles and flags, finder flip, role validation, git root, trust, scope, empty-diff exit, pin, snapshot, fit, mode and langs, prompts, prompt ceiling, run-record init, finder, verifier, survey completion, report, finalize, exit. Same order as Go.\n  - `reviewExitError` priority is the same: a finalize error, then exit 1 at `--max-severity`, then exit 4 for a partial run.\n  - The snapshot is deleted on every exit before the run record exists.\n- **Defaults:** every numeric default equals Go's constants (16/40 turns, 10m/25m deadline, 200k/100k quick sizes, 80 lines / 4 files for interactive, 8 verifier turns, 60k snippet).\n- **Scope OIDs:** `base_oid` and `merge_base_oid` came only from branch scope in Go. Dropping them is deliberate change 23.\n- **Verifier** (`src/verify/verify.ts`): concurrency 4, cap and ledger checks before each call, every error becomes an undecided verdict, a refutation without grounding fails open, an ungrounded recalibration is cleared, input order is kept, and the assessment is recomputed. The confidence floor uses the quick floor only with `--quick`. Equivalent to `verify.go` and `Verdict.Gates()`.\n- **Finder** (`src/review/find.ts`): the no-final-call path with zero findings now goes through `validate`, but it produces the same result as Go's literal.\n- **Gate:** `bootstrap.ts` and `hook.ts` match `bootstrap.go` and `hook.go` branch for branch. The one difference, a hook with no trailing newline getting one, is deliberate change 19. The offer is skipped under `--error-format json` and when `GIT_INDEX_FILE` is set, as in Go.\n\n**Findings:**\n\n1. **Review flag help defaults are hardcoded instead of coming from `src/config/defaults.ts`.** This breaks the AGENTS.md rule that review flag defaults should use that module.\n   - Where: `src/cli/review-flags.ts:86-94`, plus the turn constants at `:49-50`. The survey and quick constants at `src/cli/review.ts:94-98` have the same issue.\n   - What goes wrong: the help strings literally say `default 10m`, `default 3000000`, `default 25` and `default 4`. The runtime reads `DEFAULT_LIMITS`. If someone changes `DEFAULT_LIMITS.deadline` or `max_verified`, the starter comments and runtime follow, but `--help` keeps showing the old value, and no test catches it.\n   - Go reference: `cli.go addReviewFlags` built help from the same constants the runtime used (`shortDuration(defaultDeadline)`, `defaultMaxTotalTokens`).\n\n2. **Several gate-offer branches have no test.**\n   - Where: `src/gate/bootstrap.ts:59-64` and `:73-79`, `test/gate/bootstrap.ts`, `test/cli/gate-offer.ts`.\n   - Untested paths:\n     - A foreign hook that can't be appended to, which should print the hint once.\n     - A foreign hook that can be appended to, where the user agrees to the append prompt.\n     - Consent with a hook that can't be appended to, which records `enabled` and prints the manual line.\n     - A repo whose decision is `enabled` but whose hook is missing, which should reinstall it (`installStep(o, false)`).\n   - Go reference: `internal/gate/bootstrap_test.go` didn't cover these either, so this isn't a regression. But these are the paths that write into someone else's hook.\n\nEverything else checked out."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":157192,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018gF4SKTMT76p6W4DKSyVyJ","agent_id":"a65d44a24feed96f9","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","uuid":"97bec708-38f3-4fbd-83ba-832f26639a8f","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:07:22.775Z","request_id":"req_011ChM6QZTVNML39CnrMDK62","subagent_type":"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose","task_description":"Review review cmd/verify/gate"}
