{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM6SM79f1WRoYHCHi9GQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No solid correctness bugs, unlisted parity breaks, or important test gaps in the reviewed files.\n\nOne limit on the parity check: at c0b539fc the Go client built the wire format through the Fantasy library and its SDKs (`internal/llm/provider.go:85-113`). None of that code is in this repo, so I couldn't compare request bodies, SSE handling or stop reasons against Go source. I checked them against spec 06 §2.6.2, §2.6.3, §2.8.2, §2.8.3, §2.9 and §2.10 instead. The parts that did exist in Go matched:\n- Anthropic base URL trimming (`provider.go:104`).\n- Disjoint Anthropic usage (`provider.go:135-162`).\n- Schema cloning (`agent.go:747`).\n- Auto tool choice (`agent.go:209`).\n- The binding fake's prefix rule (`thinking_binding_test.go:73-109`).\n\nWhat matched the spec:\n- **`anthropic.ts` requests:** the URL, request body and alternating-role grouping (the thinking-only message is dropped after grouping). Signed, redacted and unsigned thinking replay; non-object tool input becomes `{}`; the full `input_schema` with `required` defaulted (#21); the `claude-mythos-preview` thinking field.\n- **`anthropic.ts` stream:** decoding by block index and the `tool_use` input fallback chain. `message_delta` usage only replaces fields that are present and non-null. The finish map and raw-reason exposure; incomplete stream when `message_stop` or the stop reason is missing; error-event retry classes; a malformed event is not retried.\n- **`responses.ts` requests:** system-prompt mode by model, reasoning never replayed, `store:false`, and no `previous_response_id`, `include` or `reasoning`.\n- **`responses.ts` stream:** tool calls emitted only for opened function calls, the finish mapping with and without a tool call, and `response.failed` / `error` never retried. It reads to the end of the stream after the terminal event.\n- **`usage.ts`:** cached tokens are subtracted once (#13); the reasoning-above-output rule.\n- **`client.ts`:** only the two adapter registrations changed in this diff. Redirect refusal (#8), the 32 KiB error-body cap (#9), timeout handling and abort re-throw are unchanged.\n- **Tests:** they cover the spec §5 rows for these adapters, either here or in `test/cli/review-anthropic.ts` and `test/cli/review-responses.ts`. That includes the interrupted Anthropic stream being retried and captured, a 401 mapping to auth, the 500 that is never retried, and the binding and DeepSeek fakes.\n\nOne cosmetic issue, not a bug: `src/llm/anthropic.ts:279`. An Anthropic stream `error` event with no `error` object (`{\"type\":\"error\"}`) makes `JSON.stringify(undefined)` return `undefined`. The error message then reads `stream error: undefined`. It is still classified correctly as not retryable. There's no Go code to compare, since this handling lived in Fantasy."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":127551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1285,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01T6H39Mzrb9HTVEpUPxaMw9","agent_id":"a2d564e3db2c159ee","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","uuid":"de212b0a-5330-4607-9241-2304d586d273","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:07:43.798Z","request_id":"req_011ChM6SLo3qpYTBEJRrX7yY","subagent_type":"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose","task_description":"Review LLM adapters"}
