{"duration_api_ms":674551,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"88028451-5f39-411f-b6c1-a60f530aedf7","total_cost_usd":6.010610200000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2894,"cache_read_input_tokens":181467,"output_tokens":1716,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2894,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":91578,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1205},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":246,"outputTokens":65534,"cacheReadInputTokens":10834021,"cacheCreationInputTokens":457934,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":6.010610200000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":38954,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":377110,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":80824,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwu66v71-82aadd1d"},"subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":3},"started_in_background":3,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"ed3d-basic-agents:opus-general-purpose":3}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I found three things worth fixing in the merged change and wrote them to `.redeye/findings.md`, most severe first. The full CI gate passes: lint, typecheck, `npm test`, the schema check, and `check:pack`. No test state leaked into the checkout.\n\n1. **Secret files can leak into snapshots (security, Linux only).** Snapshot capture (`src/snapshot/snapshot.ts:165-174`) gets its exclude list from `denylistedUntracked`. That function silently drops file names that aren't valid UTF-8. So an untracked file like `\\xff.pem` gets no exclude, is committed into the snapshot ref, and can reach the model through `grep_repo`. The Go version matched the denylist on raw bytes and excluded these files. Deliberate change 24 covers skipping such names from review, not capturing them. No test covers this; it needs one that runs only on Linux, because macOS refuses these names.\n2. **Snapshots may break on older Git.** `src/snapshot/snapshot.ts:267` and `:290` pass `--end-of-options` to `git rev-parse`. Git didn't accept that until about 2.43, though I couldn't confirm the exact version: this machine only has 2.49 and 2.50, which both accept it. On Debian 12 or Ubuntu 22.04, every capture would fail with \"repository has no commits\", and `runs checkout` would fail too. The Go code didn't pass this flag, and it adds nothing here.\n3. **`review --help` shows hardcoded defaults.** `src/cli/review-flags.ts:86-94` writes values like \"default 10m\" and \"default 3000000\" into the help text. AGENTS.md says review flag defaults should come from `src/config/defaults.ts`, as the runtime's do. If a default changes there, the help text goes stale and no test catches it.\n\nEverything else checked out:\n- **Byte-identical to Go:** the prompt templates, the pre-commit hook script, and the skill asset.\n- **Same as Go:** the gate bootstrap, the order of steps in `review`, the verifier, and the numeric defaults.\n- **Matches the spec:** the `responses` and `anthropic` adapters. The Go request-building code lived in an outside library that isn't in the repo, so these were compared against the spec, not Go.\n- **Matches the M6 cutover checklist:** the CI workflow and packaging changes.\n\nI left out two minor items: `runs checkout` error messages for a missing or corrupt `meta.json` differ from Go's (same exit code), and four rarely hit branches of the gate offer have no tests (Go didn't test them either).","ttft_ms":7366,"type":"result","duration_ms":15455,"uuid":"9b1d183e-432b-41c2-b5c2-5f6e1e9f5181","ttft_stream_ms":827,"time_to_request_ms":84,"first_content_frame_ms":828,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":3,"model_usage_since_last_result":{},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-09T10:07:39.368Z"}
